  "id": "Compound::DB00306 - Gene::2556",
  "verbalization": "Talbutal is likely to interact with Gabra3 through a series of molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that Talbutal binds to Gabre, which in turn participates in Gaba-a Receptor Activity, and this activity is mediated by Gabra3. Similarly, Talbutal binds to Gabra6, which participates in Benzodiazepine Receptor Activity, also mediated by Gabra3. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Talbutal influences Gaba-a and Benzodiazepine receptor activities, both of which are associated with Gabra3. The overlapping involvement of Gabra3 in these different receptor activities suggests a possible role in the regulation of multiple neurotransmitter systems. The integration of these pathways implies that Talbutal may modulate receptor function through distinct binding sites on Gabra3, thereby influencing its physiological effects.",
